# Vault conventions

Adaptations to standard [Johnny Decimal](https://johnnydecimal.com/) for this project.

## Node structure

A JD node (e.g. `32.01`) can be either:

- **A file**: `32.01 interviews.md` — a single document
- **A directory**: `32.01 interviews/` — a collection of related documents

### Directory nodes

When a node is a directory, its contents are **tertiary-numbered files** of the form `XX.YY.ZZ name with spaces`:

```
32 user research/
└── 32.01 interviews/
    ├── 32.01.01 first person 2026-03-20.md
    ├── 32.01.02 another person 2026-04-15.md
    └── assets/
        └── call-recording-notes.png
```

The tertiary number establishes ordering and identity within the collection, consistent with how two-tiered node numbers work at the category level.

### Depth constraint

Beyond the tertiary file level, **only one more level of subdirectory is allowed** — strictly for assets (images, attachments, supporting files). No deeper nesting.

```
# Fine
32.01 interviews/assets/screenshot.png
33.04 roadmap targets/33.04.01 some focused problem.md

# Bad
32.01 interviews/2026/march/notes/draft.md
```

## Frontmatter

Every vault document must include YAML frontmatter with a `description` field:

```markdown
---
description: short summary of what the document covers
---
```

This description is used by the auto-generated vault index (`00.00 index.md`). When you add or modify a vault document, run `generate-vault-index` to regenerate the index. The `vault-index-check` pre-commit hook will reject commits where the index is out of date.

Directory nodes should place their frontmatter in an `overview.md` file inside the directory.

## Cross-references

Use `[[wikilink]]` syntax for cross-references between vault documents (Obsidian-compatible). Reference by filename without path:

```markdown
See [[20.02 dependency injection]] for details.
```

## Linear issue references

Reference Linear tickets as markdown links using the full URL:

```markdown
See [{{ module_name[:3].upper() }}-474](https://linear.app/<your-linear-workspace>/issue/{{ module_name[:3].upper() }}-474) for details.
```

The URL format is `https://linear.app/<your-linear-workspace>/issue/{{ module_name[:3].upper() }}-XXX`.

## Naming

All names are **lowercase** (except proper nouns or technical terms). JD-numbered items use spaces, not hyphens, since the decimal prefix already makes them unique and unambiguous.

- Area directories: `XX-XX name` (e.g. `30-39 product`)
- Category directories: `XX name` (e.g. `32 user research`)
- Node files/directories: `XX.XX name with spaces` (e.g. `30.01 engagement first design`)
- Tertiary nodes: `XX.YY.ZZ name with spaces` (e.g. `33.04.01 some focused problem`)
